+# Proposed GitHub Actions release checks — approval pending
+
+No `.github/workflows` file has been created. This is the concrete job design for approval, not an installed pipeline. Resolve the documented regression failures before treating any job as a release gate.
+
+## Triggers and isolation
+
+Pull requests and pushes to the protected main branch; cancel superseded runs for the same ref. Read-only repository permissions, no production credentials, no production seed accounts. Pin checkout/setup/artifact actions to reviewed commit SHAs when implementing. Use Node 24/npm 11.6.2 and `npm ci`. Cache npm downloads, not mutable build outputs or databases. Keep signing jobs separate, protected and unavailable to untrusted PRs.
+
+## Jobs
+
+| Job                     | Host / dependencies                                                                                                   | Commands and artifacts                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                    |
+| ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
+| Static + unit           | Linux                                                                                                                 | `npm run format:check`, `check:foundation`, `check:parity`, `check:redesign`, `audit:ui`, `lint`, `typecheck`, `npm test -- --maxWorkers=2`. Upload logs and audit JSON even on failure.                                                                                                                                  |
+| Integration             | Linux + disposable PostgreSQL service; CREATEDB test role, loopback access, health check; pg_dump/pg_restore binaries | Set only `TEST_DATABASE_URL` to the service test database; `npm run test:integration -- --maxWorkers=2`. Tests own migrations and rollback. Never enable retained-database mode to hide rollback failures. Upload logs; service is destroyed with the job.                                                                |
+| Browser + accessibility | Linux, after shared build; install Chrome/Playwright OS dependencies                                                  | `PLAYWRIGHT_CHANNEL=chrome npm run test:web:browser`, then `npx playwright test --config=playwright.shell.config.ts`. Use local mock transport for shell scenarios. Archive traces, failures and axe evidence.                                                                                                            |
+| Visual                  | Pinned host/image, Chrome and fonts; mock server on 5197                                                              | `npx playwright test --config=playwright.redesign.config.ts` without `--update-snapshots`. Current candidate baselines were captured on macOS: approve a separately named Linux baseline rather than silently comparing cross-OS font rasterization. Archive expected/actual/diff. Baseline changes require human review. |
+| Web artifact            | Linux, static/unit/integration/browser dependencies                                                                   | `npm run build`, `npm run check:redesign-budget`; upload web dist and SHA-256 manifest. Build is not deployment.                                                                                                                                                                                                          |
+| Windows desktop         | Windows runner, Rust/MSVC/WebView2 build prerequisites                                                                | `npm ci`, `npm run build:desktop`; upload unsigned installer/app checksums and logs. No claim of installed-app or peripheral qualification.                                                                                                                                                                               |
+| macOS desktop           | macOS runner, Xcode/Rust                                                                                              | `npm ci`, `npm run build -w @inventory/desktop -- --bundles app`; upload app archive/checksums. Add DMG/sign/notarize only in a protected release job with a verified noninteractive packaging strategy; local DMG currently fails Finder automation.                                                                     |
+| Mobile parity           | Linux JS export; independent of desktop release qualification                                                         | `npm run build:mobile`; retain export logs. Native signed binary/device jobs require a separate approved setup.                                                                                                                                                                                                           |
+
+## Release gates outside CI
+
+Windows/macOS clean install/upgrade; real API authentication and scoped workflows; printer/scanner; deep links; vault interruption/restart; expired grants and sync conflicts; VoiceOver/NVDA/TalkBack. Record artifact hash, hardware/OS, role and actual results. Signing, deployment and automatic updates are not authorized by approving this test workflow.
+
+Approval requested for implementing this job design after review; no action or provider setup is assumed approved by this document.
